{
 "question": "What does an image already on a page give the importer, without its picture?",
 "how": "Read on 2026-11-06 in the oracle's site frame, out of edit mode: every image on Services, About and Home at a frame 1242 wide (Demo and Contact have none). Overlay, Lightbox, the focal point, Shape and Stretch appear on no saved page, so those were set on a new image on the probe page, never saved, and read in the editor's preview. The link was read in edit mode on the same image.",
 "markers": {
  "mode": "the content-fit or content-fill class on the picture's element, and data-is-mask-applied with data-shape-mask for Shape",
  "stretch": "data-is-image-stretched on the root",
  "focal": "data-media-focal-point, x,y from 0 to 1",
  "pictureSize": "data-image-dimensions on the img",
  "overlay": "the fluidImageOverlay element's opacity, background color and blend mode",
  "lightbox": "a button with data-lightbox-theme around the picture",
  "link": "an a with class sqs-block-image-link around the picture, its href the link's",
  "phone": "data-bpo, empty on all 15 saved images"
 },
 "shapeBox": "A Shape that isn't stretched has a box of 1:1 or 2:3 on the saved pages. 2:3 for narrow-horizontal-stacked-pills and arched-window, whose pictures are also 2:3, and 1:1 for rabbet and one flower, whose pictures are square. One flower holds a 2:3 picture (2533x3800) in a square, so the picture alone doesn't set it. A pick in the editor keeps the square (IMAGESHAPES.json). The rule behind these is not measured, so the importer takes the box it reads.",
